Thank you: review confirmed the guard rejects every compound form at the top level. It confirmed this repository's check and `retry_files` stay eligible, and that the non-targeted retries are unchanged.

`singleBunTest(cfg.retryFiles)` checks the template before the filenames are substituted (~src/gates/run.ts:336). `quoteRetryFiles` quotes for an unquoted shell context, so a template such as `bun test "{files}"` passes the check. A failing test file named `test/x"; true #.test.ts` then expands to `bun test "'./test/x"; true #.test.ts'"`, whose exit status comes from `true`. Review reproduced this with real Bun: the original failure had complete attribution, and the targeted retry returned `ok: true` without re-running the failing test.

Fix:
- Accept `retry_files` only when `{files}` appears exactly once as a standalone, unquoted shell word.
- Also run `singleBunTest` on the expanded command before executing it on the targeted-only path; refuse with a skip reason if it fails.

Add this test from review (adjust helpers to fit), make it pass and don't weaken it:

```ts
test("a quoted retry placeholder cannot turn a failing test into a shell success", async () => {
  const f = fixture();
  try {
    const file = 'test/x"; true #.test.ts';
    writeFileSync(
      join(f.cwd, file),
      'import { test, expect } from "bun:test"; test("still fails", () => expect(1).toBe(2));',
    );
    const check = {
      ...testCheck,
      run: 'bun test --reporter=junit --reporter-outfile="$LIMITLESS_GATE_REPORT"',
    };
    const cfg = { ...config, checks: [check], retryFiles: 'bun test "{files}"' };
    await confinementScope.run(fakeConfinement, async () => {
      const run = await runLocalGates(f.cwd, cfg, signal, { env: bunEnv });
      const original = run.checks[0];
      if (!original) throw new Error("Missing original check");
      expect(original.ok).toBe(false);
      expect(original.failureAttributionComplete).toBe(true);
      expect(original.failedFiles).toEqual([file]);
      const retries = await retryFailures(
        [{ check, original }],
        f.cwd,
        cfg,
        signal,
        undefined,
        (retry) => runLocalGates(f.cwd, retry, signal, { env: bunEnv }),
        true,
      );
      expect(retries.get(original)?.ok ?? false).toBe(false);
    });
  } finally {
    f.close();
  }
});

```

