original.detail:
Thank you: review confirmed the core change.
- Build, needs-human, review, CI-fix and conflict deliveries all pass through the fresh tree check (~src/pipeline/engine.ts:3090), which repeats after delivery merges (~3124).
- The verified-draft fallback checks its explicit SHA; workers check the committed candidate before pushing.
- The verify-change exception covers only the author's edits; repairs are audited against the original head.
- `workflows` is parsed from requester text only, the matcher is single and exported, and disabling the guard makes the 8 negative cases fail.

**P1: manual landing still pushes ungranted workflow changes.** `scripts/land-pr.sh` checks private strings (~line 118), then pushes the pinned commit (~135) without the workflow guard. The issue asks for every push path, including `scripts/`. Scenario: from an existing PR, commit `.github/workflows/ungranted.yml` locally and run the script without a grant. The clean-worktree and privacy checks pass and the push proceeds. Review reproduced it with the real script up to an intercepted push.

Fix: run the same exported guard against the exact candidate SHA the script pushes, before any transport. The grant must be the operator's own: an explicit `--allow workflows` argument to the script, never text from the PR. On refusal, name the files and the grant in the message. Document it where the script is described.

Add this test from review (adjust helpers to fit), make it pass and don't weaken it:

