This is the last review round. The freshness sentinel, the `--` refusal and the fabricated-`met` refusal are right, and each test fails without its fix.

One regression, reproduced: the round's prose scan (~233, with the rejection at ~213) treats any occurrence of 'Factory gate' in a row's evidence as a citation, so a sandbox-blocked verifier quoting `bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title'` can't get substitution even with a valid passing factory record for that exact test. Validate only the structured citation fields (`gateEvidence` and the covering-test record reference) against factory records for the same SHA. Remove the prose scanner, the exact prose-citation consumer (~195) and the recursive eligibility reconstruction (~240): the binding doesn't need them, and the issue's budget was about 120 lines against 562 in this PR. Free text in `evidence` is never authority, in either direction.

Add these regression tests from review (they fail on this PR; adjust helpers, don't weaken them):

```ts
test("quoted factory-like test titles do not prevent covering-test binding", () => {
  const run = coveringRun();
  run.name = "Factory gate literal title";
  if (!run.result) throw new Error("missing result");
  run.result.command = "bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title' './x.test.ts'";
  run.result.coveringTest = { file: run.file, name: run.name };
  const value = {
    ...requested,
    criteria: requested.criteria.map((c) => ({
      ...c,
      evidence: "Attempted bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title' x.test.ts: EPERM in sandbox",
      covering_tests: [{ file: run.file, name: run.name }],
