original.detail:
Thank you: review confirmed the rollback ordering and durable intent, the recovery of consecutive `restored` journals, reconciliation after every successful deploy (same-SHA and `--now`) with non-canonical labels, release-following while idle, exactly-once execution across a restart, and the default-off compatibility.

One P1, reproduced: every nonzero `launchctl print` is taken to mean 'unloaded' (~322). If inspection fails (for example 'Operation not permitted') while the executor is still loaded, shutdown skips bootout, runs `disable` (which doesn't stop a running process), and returns success. Rollback then restores the checkout (~922), and intent recovery (~382) does the same. Distinguish confirmed absence (the specific 'could not find service' result) from any other failure. On unknown state, refuse to touch the checkout and print the existing recovery instructions.

Add these regression tests from review (they fail on this PR; adjust helpers, don't weaken them):

```ts
for (const recovery of [false, true]) {
  test(`executor inspection failure refuses checkout changes (recovery: ${recovery})`, async () => {
    const f = executorSetup();
    if (recovery)
      writeFileSync(
        f.intent,
        JSON.stringify({
          phase: "rollback",
          label: f.label,
          path: f.path,
          previous: "previous",
          target: "next",
        }),
      );
    const command = f.opts.command;
    f.opts.command = async (args, opts) => {
      if (args[0] === "launchctl" && args[1] === "print") {
        f.calls.push(args.join(" "));
        return { exitCode: 1, stdout: "", stderr: "Operation not permitted" };
      }
      if (args[0] === "bun" && args[1] === "run") throw new Error("gate failed");
      return command(args, opts);
    };
    const error = String(await deploy(7400, "feature", false, { ...f.opts, executor: true }).catch((e) => e));
    expect(f.calls).not.toContain("git checkout -q --detach previous");
    if (recovery) expect(f.calls.some((call) => call.startsWith("git "))).toBe(false);
    expect(error).toContain(`launchctl bootout ${f.service}`);
    expect(error).toContain(`launchctl disable ${f.service}`);
    expect(existsSync(f.intent)).toBe(true);
  });
}
```

