original.detail:
Thank you: round 1 fixed adjacent references, details truncation and prose mentions, and the pre-round code fails six of the new tests.

A focused review of the resolver reproduced six more P2s, all from hand-parsing Markdown. One is an end-to-end false success: a fence whose delimiter is longer than an inner fence makes a hidden `## Hidden` end the section, and the run passes after checking only the first unit. The others: a mismatched tilde fence; HTML comments that end sections or import references; setext and indented headings that are missed or treated as duplicates; `</details >` with a space not closing; and partial multi-paragraph list items.

Each round finds another construct, and a miss here can drop a requirement. As the spec's owner I'm replacing #974's "code fences and `<details>` blocks are left out" with a fail-closed rule.

**Section references (b) and the ticket's `## The original intent` section** may contain only:
- ATX headings (`#`–`######`, at most three leading spaces, followed by a space or the end of the line, where a closing `#` sequence counts only when preceded by a space);
- list items, including their indented continuation lines and paragraphs;
- paragraphs, blockquotes and table rows;
- blank lines.
Any other construct inside the scanned range refuses resolution before any model call (`failed`, "unsupported Markdown in the intent: <construct>; normalize the ticket"). That covers a fence line (three or more backticks or tildes), an HTML block or comment (a line starting with `<`), a `<details>` block, a setext underline (a `=`-only or `-`-only line directly under a paragraph line), an indented code block (four or more spaces outside a list) and a heading indented four or more spaces. Scan line by line from the referenced heading, so the first unsupported line refuses before any later heading can end the section. Remove the details and fence exclusion code.

**Heading matching:** count ATX headings only, in the whole parent. If the parent has a setext heading whose text equals the referenced heading, refuse as ambiguous. `## Goal` and `## Goal#` are different headings.

**Quote sources (a):**
- Parse `From …:` lead-ins as physical lines before any paragraph normalization. The nearest preceding lead-in applies, including one directly after prose.
- A list-item unit includes all its continuation paragraphs, so a quote of only its first paragraph is "not a whole source unit".
- A source may contain fences, HTML or details outside the quoted unit: lines inside a fence or HTML comment never form units, using CommonMark's rule that the closing fence uses the same character and is at least as long. An unclosed fence or comment refuses "unresolvable source".

**Tests:** Codex's 16 regressions are below. Where one expects content to be excluded or ignored, the expected outcome is now a refusal with the unsupported-Markdown reason, and no model call. Keep the end-to-end case: with the nested-fence parent the run must not succeed. Update docs and the spec text the PR quotes, and name this rule change in the PR body.

Scope: the change is already about 606 lines against the 250 stop. This rule should remove code; report the final count.

```ts

test.each([
  ["short backtick closer", "````md\n```\n## Hidden\n- Hidden.\n````"],
  ["different fence character", "```md\n~~~\n## Hidden\n- Hidden.\n```"],
])("review regression: %s cannot truncate a referenced section", async (_name, fence) => {
  const units = await resolve(
    `#1's "Goal" section`,
    `## Goal\n- Before.\n\n${fence}\n\n- After.\n\n## End\n- Outside.`,
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before.", "After."]);
});

test("review regression: a reference inside a longer fence creates no units", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(
    `> Before.\n\n\`\`\`\`md\n\`\`\`\n#1's "Other" section\n\`\`\`\``,
    "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n## Other\n- Other.",
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before."]);
});

test("review regression: a commented heading cannot truncate a referenced section", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(
    `#1's "Goal" section`,
    "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n<!--\n## Hidden\n- Hidden.\n-->\n\n- After.\n\n## End",
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before.", "After."]);
});

test("review regression: a commented reference creates no units", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(
    `> Before.\n\n<!--\n#1's "Other" section\n-->`,
    "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n## Other\n- Other.",
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before."]);
});

test.each([
  ["setext", "Goal\n===="],
  ["indented ATX", "  ## Goal"],
])("review regression: a visible %s duplicate heading is ambiguous", async (_name, heading) => {
  await expect(resolve(`#1's "Goal" section`, `## Goal\n- Before.\n\n${heading}\n- Other.`)).rejects.toThrow(
    "does not name exactly one heading",
  );
});

test("review regression: an attached trailing hash is part of the heading text", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(`#1's "Goal" section`, "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n## Goal#\n- Outside.");
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before."]);
});

test.each([
  ["setext", "End\n==="],
  ["indented ATX", "  ## End"],
])("review regression: a %s heading ends the referenced section", async (_name, heading) => {
  const units = await resolve(`#1's "Goal" section`, `## Goal\n- Before.\n\n${heading}\n- Outside.`);
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before."]);
});

test("review regression: adjacent source lines validate against the last named source", async () => {
  await expect(
    resolve("From #1:\nFrom docs/PLAN.md (docs):\n\n> Parent only.", "- Parent only."),
  ).rejects.toThrow("quote is not a whole source unit");
});

test("review regression: a source line after context still selects the file", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(
    "Context for the quote.\nFrom docs/PLAN.md:\n\n> The queue skips untrusted issues.",
    "- Parent only.",
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => [u.text, u.sources])).toEqual([
    ["The queue skips untrusted issues.", ["docs/PLAN.md"]],
  ]);
});

test("review regression: whitespace in a details closing tag cannot hide later units", async () => {
  const units = await resolve(
    `#1's "Goal" section`,
    "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n<details>\n- Hidden.\n</details >\n\n- After.\n\n## End",
  );
  expect(units.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before.", "After."]);
});

test.each(["#1", "docs/PLAN.md"])(
  "review regression: a quote cannot omit the second paragraph of a %s list item",
  async (source) => {
    const body = "- Retry failed deliveries.\n\n  Never retry a permanent rejection.\n";
    await expect(
      resolveIntent(snapshot(`From ${source}:\n\n> Retry failed deliveries.`, body), async () => body),
    ).rejects.toThrow("quote is not a whole source unit");
  },
);
test("review regression: a heading inside a longer fence cannot let acceptance pass early", async () => {
  const t = await setup({
    parent: "## Goal\n- Before.\n\n````md\n```\n## Hidden\n- Hidden.\n````\n\n- After.\n\n## End\n- Outside.",
    ticket: `## The original intent\n#1's "Goal" section`,
  });
  t.reply(() => ({
    structured: output([{ unit: "U1", verdict: "met", tests: ["passes"] }]),
  }));
  expect(await t.execute()).toBe("needs_human");
  expect(t.state()?.acceptance?.manifest?.map((u) => u.text)).toEqual(["Before.", "After."]);
  expect(t.outcome().units.map((u) => [u.unit, u.verdict])).toEqual([
    ["U1", "met"],
    ["U2", "not_assessed"],
  ]);
});


```

